# Prettier baseline — POLICY, hand-edited, never regenerated (#483).
#
# `make check` never ran Prettier, so 152 of the 352 files it considers had
# drifted by the time this gate landed. Reformatting them all is not
# available: it churns 98 files under web/src and scores 74.4% (314/422)
# against the 80% changed-line gate, because re-wrapped lines count as
# changed lines and the sweep takes untested files along with covered ones.
#
# So these are pinned and everything else is gated. Two rules:
#
#   * Never add a line here. A newly-drifted file is a failure, not a pin —
#     run `cd web && npx prettier --write <path>` instead.
#   * Delete a line as soon as its file is formatted. The gate FAILS on a
#     stale pin, on purpose: a list that only ever grows is an amnesty, not
#     a baseline. Same contract as `granularity.known_coarse` in
#     data/authors/manifest.yaml.
#
# This is NOT .prettierignore. `npm run format` honours that file, so a pin
# there could never be fixed by the formatter and the baseline could never
# shrink. Genuine exclusions (generated output, the codegen-owned files of
# #486) live there instead.
#
# Count when landed: 150. Expect it to fall.
